{
  "_comment": [
    "The DDS bridge's configuration. Two sections, read by two different things.",
    "",
    "dds.ddsmodule is the DDS Enabler's own - domain, QoS, threads, logging.",
    "dds.ngsild is the broker's - which topic becomes which entity attribute.",
    "",
    "A topic must already exist in the DDS system. The broker is a participant",
    "in that system, not the author of it: topics and types are compiled into",
    "the applications on the domain, and a topic named here that nobody",
    "publishes is simply a topic that never delivers.",
    "",
    "The mapping below is the one the `demo` profile of docker-compose-dds.yml",
    "publishes: the ROS 2 demo talker's /chatter, which on the domain is the",
    "topic `rt/chatter`. Replace it with yours - the shape is one entry per",
    "topic, and the entity is created from the entry alone, before any sample",
    "has arrived:",
    "",
    "  \"rt/pose\": {",
    "    \"entityId\":   \"urn:ngsi-ld:Robot:1\",",
    "    \"entityType\": \"Robot\",",
    "    \"attribute\":  \"pose\"",
    "  }",
    "",
    "The mapping is read in both directions. A sample on the topic becomes the",
    "attribute's value; a PATCH of the attribute is published as a sample on",
    "the topic."
  ],

  "dds": {
    "ddsmodule": {
      "dds": { "domain": 0 },
      "specs": { "threads": 4, "logging": { "verbosity": "warning" } }
    },

    "ngsild": {
      "typesDirectory": "/opt/seamware/etc/dds-types",

      "topics": {
        "rt/chatter": {
          "entityId":   "urn:ngsi-ld:Talker:1",
          "entityType": "Talker",
          "attribute":  "message"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
